 set <MATH_0002>. Consider the functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>-algebras<MATHSEG_0002>\ndefined by the rule\n<MATHSEG_0003>if there exist <MATHSEG_0004> such that <MATHSEG_0005> and <MATHSEG_0006>else<MATHSEG_0007>\nGeometrically <MATH_0003> means there exists a quasi-compact open neighbourhood\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006>.\nLet <MATH_0007> be the full\nsubcategory consisting of schemes <MATH_0008> which have an affine open covering\n<MATH_0009> with <MATH_0010> for all <MATH_0011>. Then <MATH_0012>\nsatisfies [0], [1], [2], [3], and [4] but not [5]. Namely, over\n<MATH_0013>\nthere exists an object <MATH_0014> which is versal at <MATH_0015> but not\nat any other point. Details omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c209e59e1f2e5bb848f3af569fdba12d20951840bea938482b10abfe461806a", "unit_id": "tag:07XR:statement"}
