: "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed52563a6afc533f515ea24edb9f3f777f01e0cacf514757ccb845fd38160ae0", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:58e6fc4fc22f90935578e98ea16e1c75009b60ecaea04c0ea8f6eee6e0f8ca7e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e856ea903656afa66d63ef29466ac5e5fed5da5e6445e6b231404b7522aa57a9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a <MATH_0003>-morphism of categories\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0004>. Consider the following property\n<MATHSEG_0001>for all fields <MATHSEG_0002> of finite type over <MATHSEG_0003> and all <MATHSEG_0004> the<MATHSEG_0005>map <MATHSEG_0006> of predeformation categories is smooth<MATHSEG_0007>\nWe formulate some lemmas around this concept. First we link it with\n(openness of) versality.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f7d7fdd6ae074617bbff86eb012e04ff4b0c9a7c8d1adefa825d9678a297b88", "unit_id": "tag:07XP:prose-0003"}
